### FASE 5: Gestión de Entregas a Clientes
**Objetivo:** Rastrear entregas de productos a clientes

#### Paso 5.1: Crear Modelos de Entregas
**Archivos a crear:**
- `backend/models/Delivery.js` (CREAR)
- `backend/models/DeliveryDetail.js` (CREAR)
- `backend/models/index.js` (MODIFICAR)

**Modelo Delivery:**
```javascript
{
  id: INTEGER (PK, auto-increment),
  delivery_number: STRING (único, auto: "ENT-YYYYMMDD-0001"),
  sale_id: INTEGER (FK → Sale),
  customer_id: INTEGER (FK → Customer),
  warehouse_id: INTEGER (FK → Warehouse),
  delivery_date: DATE,
  scheduled_date: DATE,
  delivery_address: TEXT,
  delivery_city: STRING,
  delivery_state: STRING,
  contact_name: STRING,
  contact_phone: STRING,
  status: ENUM ('pending', 'in_transit', 'delivered', 'failed', 'cancelled'),
  delivery_method: ENUM ('pickup', 'courier', 'own_fleet', 'shipping_company'),
  tracking_number: STRING,
  carrier: STRING (nombre de transportadora),
  notes: TEXT,
  delivered_by: INTEGER (FK → User),
  delivered_at: TIMESTAMP,
  signature_image_url: STRING (opcional: foto de firma de recepción),
  created_by: INTEGER (FK → User),
  timestamps: true
}
```

**Modelo DeliveryDetail:**
```javascript
{
  id: INTEGER (PK, auto-increment),
  delivery_id: INTEGER (FK → Delivery),
  sale_detail_id: INTEGER (FK → SaleDetail),
  product_id: INTEGER (FK → Product),
  presentation_id: INTEGER (FK → ProductPresentation),
  package_quantity_delivered: INTEGER,
  loose_units_delivered: INTEGER,
  timestamps: true
}
```

**Relaciones:**
- Delivery → Sale (Many to One)
- Delivery → Customer (Many to One)
- Delivery → Warehouse (Many to One)
- Delivery → User (delivered_by, created_by)
- Delivery → DeliveryDetail (One to Many)
- DeliveryDetail → SaleDetail, Product, Presentation

#### Paso 5.2: Crear Controlador de Entregas
**Archivos a crear:**
- `backend/controllers/delivery.controller.js` (CREAR)
- `backend/routes/delivery.routes.js` (CREAR)
